“Misunderstood” is probably closer to what you mean.

A person can be read badly because others see the behavior but not the motive, context, history, or internal logic behind it. But being misunderstood also doesn’t make every action harmless. Intent, impact, and interpretation are three different layers.

A stronger formulation might be:

“I’m not trying to be a bad person. I’ve been misunderstood, and I’m still responsible for making myself easier to understand.”

That keeps both truths: you don’t have to accept someone else’s worst interpretation of you, and you still get to refine how you show up.